You are building Mandate. Read PRD.md (FR-/SEC-/RT- IDs) and DEV-PROCESS.md before starting any task. Do not infer requirements that are not written there. Do not edit PRD.md or DEV-PROCESS.md.

When PRD.md or DEV-PROCESS.md disagree with ARCHITECTURE.md, code, or this file, **PRD.md / DEV-PROCESS.md win**. If those files are not in the tree yet, follow ARCHITECTURE.md and restore the originals without rewriting them.

Stack: pnpm monorepo, TypeScript strict, Hono (apps/proxy), Next.js 15 App Router (apps/web), Prisma + SQLite, zod, vitest, @noble/ed25519, @modelcontextprotocol/sdk. Do not add dependencies without listing them and the reason in your final message.

Non-negotiables:
- All money is integer paise (type Paise). Never floats.
- packages/policy has NO I/O, NO LLM calls, NO Date.now() — time is passed in.
- Fail closed: unknown tool, unknown event type, unknown reason code → DENY.
- Reason codes and event types are closed enums in packages/shared. Adding one requires updating the exhaustiveness tests.
- The agent never gets a `pay` tool. Payment executes only inside apps/proxy after evaluate() returns ALLOW.
- Razorpay keys and the operator private key are never sent to apps/web or apps/agent.
- Nothing from any other codebase is copied in.

Working style:
- Before editing, state the plan in ≤ 8 bullets and list the files you will touch. Wait for confirmation on anything touching packages/policy or packages/audit.
- Write or update the test first, then the implementation, then run `pnpm test --filter <pkg>` and paste the result.
- If a task's acceptance criterion cannot be met as written, stop and say so; do not redefine it.
- Prefer small, complete diffs. Do not refactor files you were not asked to touch.
- End every task with: files changed, tests run + results, anything you were unsure about, the PRD IDs you consider satisfied.
